  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Air Simulation for the New Istanbul Airport, through Jeppesen Sanderson, Inc.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">USTDA&apos;s contribution of will partially fund a technical assistance to design the optimal airspace, runway approaches and air traffic control operating procedures for the New Istanbul Airport. The New Istanbul Airport is scheduled to open in 2018 and when completed in 2024, it will be one of the largest in the world, hosting 150 million passengers annually on flights to more than 350 destinations. Accordingly, GA Havaliman Iletmesi A.. (IGA), the concessionaire that will operate the airport for 25-years, is seeking technical assistance to ensure that the airspace operates at sufficient capacity to meet the anticipated traffic demand on the opening day in 2018. This Project Memorandum serves to update the Grant Agreement for the Terms of Reference for the Air Simulation for the New Istanbul Airport Technical Assistance (USTDA Activity No. 2016-21007A). Funding in the amount of $370.400 is being added to the Turkey Air Simulation for the New Istanbul Airport Technical Assistance.</narrative>
  </description>
